  "upload": {
    "title": "Amazon's Robots Bring the Shelves to You 🤖 #shorts",
    "description": "In Amazon fulfillment centers, drive units slide under shelving pods, lift them and carry them to workers, so people don't walk the aisles. Amazon bought the company behind the robots, Kiva Systems, for $775 million in 2012, and passed one million robots in 2025; newer robots like Proteus move autonomously around people. The twist: Kiva used to sell its robots to other retailers, but after the acquisition Amazon stopped selling them to outsiders, which set off a warehouse 'robot arms race'. The Wall Street Journal reported Amazon may soon have as many robots as human workers.",
